WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:01.601 --> 00:00:04.567
-Thank you for being here. I
want to talk about the new song.

00:00:04.567 --> 00:00:08.901
I know in Brazil, you --
the biggest star, the massive --

00:00:08.901 --> 00:00:13.167
I mean, it's insane. You went
platinum. It's crazy. I mean --

00:00:13.167 --> 00:00:15.400
-Yeah.
-And how does it differ from

00:00:15.400 --> 00:00:19.200
the U.S. and what's happening,
'cause it's happening here now.

00:00:19.200 --> 00:00:22.267
-Yeah, I started singing in
English and in Spanish.

00:00:22.267 --> 00:00:25.901
Spanish, like, four years ago
and English like one year ago.

00:00:25.901 --> 00:00:29.133
And in Brazil I have, like, 12
years of career.

00:00:29.133 --> 00:00:31.801
And everything started to grow
up very fast.

00:00:31.801 --> 00:00:34.167
But then whenever I got really
big there,

00:00:34.167 --> 00:00:37.434
I was like okay next step? I
wanna do something challenging.

00:00:37.434 --> 00:00:40.300
And somebody told me that for
Brazilians it was impossible

00:00:40.300 --> 00:00:43.968
to break up, like, to break out
of Brazil to cross over.

00:00:43.968 --> 00:00:46.467
And whenever I hear the word
"impossible,"

00:00:46.467 --> 00:00:48.334
I want to go for it.
-That's what I'm talking about.

00:00:48.334 --> 00:00:54.234
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:00:54.234 --> 00:00:55.767
-You are making history.

00:00:55.767 --> 00:00:58.534
I know that you are actually --
you're performing at Coachella.

00:00:58.534 --> 00:01:00.334
-Yeah.
-Which is massive.

00:01:00.334 --> 00:01:04.167
[ Cheers and applause ]
April 16th and the 23rd.

00:01:04.167 --> 00:01:07.334
Great line up, Billie Eilish,
Megan Thee Stallion, 21 Savage.

00:01:07.334 --> 00:01:10.234
What can people expect when they
go to see you in Coachella?

00:01:10.234 --> 00:01:13.868
-I'm -- I mean, I want to bring
Brazil to the stage

00:01:13.868 --> 00:01:15.634
and all of the favelas.

00:01:15.634 --> 00:01:18.000
I come from a community --
do you know what a favela is?

00:01:18.000 --> 00:01:19.234
-Favela? No.

00:01:19.234 --> 00:01:21.534
-Have you ever seen the movie
"City of God?"

00:01:21.534 --> 00:01:22.667
-Yes.
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:01:22.667 --> 00:01:25.467
-That's a favela.
We just party really hard.

00:01:25.467 --> 00:01:28.234
It's just a different energy,
you know?

00:01:28.234 --> 00:01:30.968
Like, whenever --
if ever you come to Brazil,

00:01:30.968 --> 00:01:33.834
you've got to bring a
little extra energy maybe.

00:01:33.834 --> 00:01:36.467
-You do?
-My friends all like to party.

00:01:36.467 --> 00:01:39.734
-So it's going to be wild?
-Yeah, I think so. Yeah.

00:01:39.734 --> 00:01:42.968
-I love that. Why not? I think
everyone wants it right now.

00:01:42.968 --> 00:01:45.267
Everyone feels like they need
it, come on we need this love.

00:01:45.267 --> 00:01:47.234
We need this energy, let's go,
let's have fun.

00:01:47.234 --> 00:01:49.667
-Yeah, by the way, I wanted to
ask you something.

00:01:49.667 --> 00:01:52.701
I love the puppies here 'cause
this --

00:01:52.701 --> 00:01:56.801
the puppy's really smart.
The Cincinnati one, the Bengals.

00:01:56.801 --> 00:01:59.067
He's the right one.
I want to bring it home.

00:01:59.067 --> 00:02:02.234
[ Laughter ]
Yeah.

00:02:02.234 --> 00:02:04.367
-You want to take that little --
-'Cause the Bengals

00:02:04.367 --> 00:02:05.968
going to win for sure.
I know for a fact.

00:02:05.968 --> 00:02:10.601
You can bet all your money
there.

00:02:10.601 --> 00:02:12.834
All your money you can bet on
Cincinnati Bengals.

00:02:12.834 --> 00:02:14.501
[ Laughter and applause ]
-I feel this.

00:02:14.501 --> 00:02:16.000
You're in my head right now.

00:02:16.000 --> 00:02:17.968
Because I've never taken
financial advice

00:02:17.968 --> 00:02:19.400
from you before --
-Yeah.

00:02:19.400 --> 00:02:21.400
[ Laughter ]
-But tonight I feel like

00:02:21.400 --> 00:02:24.234
I'm actually going to do it and
put all my money -- honey --

00:02:24.234 --> 00:02:28.200
-You know I'm also a director of
a bank in Brazil? I do that.

00:02:28.200 --> 00:02:30.033
But do you know how I know I'm
going to win --

00:02:30.033 --> 00:02:32.400
they're going to win?
I win together.

00:02:32.400 --> 00:02:36.467
'Cause one of my men is playing
there. One of my men is.

00:02:36.467 --> 00:02:39.033
-What do you mean?
-'Cause I have in each

00:02:39.033 --> 00:02:41.033
different city --
I'm traveling a lot.

00:02:41.033 --> 00:02:44.334
-Oh my God. You are -- Anitta --
don't you --

00:02:44.334 --> 00:02:47.667
[ Cheers and applause ]
-Listen.

00:02:47.667 --> 00:02:51.334
It's a lot of countries.
I was, yesterday, in Brazil.

00:02:51.334 --> 00:02:54.000
Day before, I was in L.A.
I've got to have options.

00:02:54.000 --> 00:02:59.167
So, one of my men --
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:02:59.167 --> 00:03:02.000
-How do you end up
in Cincinnati, okay?

00:03:02.000 --> 00:03:05.467
-So I was in a strip club in
Miami and I saw this guy,

00:03:05.467 --> 00:03:08.734
he was super hot and I said,
"Yo, if you don't find anyone

00:03:08.734 --> 00:03:12.701
to have sex tonight hotter than
I am, you just call me.

00:03:12.701 --> 00:03:15.501
And if I don't find anyone
hotter than you, you call me,

00:03:15.501 --> 00:03:17.400
I call you, too."
-Wow.

00:03:17.400 --> 00:03:20.367
-So, in the end of the day, we
both found.

00:03:20.367 --> 00:03:22.467
[ Laughter, applause ]

00:03:22.467 --> 00:03:25.334
-Is that how? Is that how it
works, is that how it works?

00:03:25.334 --> 00:03:28.267
-Well, I'm practical!
Some Brazil energy.

00:03:28.267 --> 00:03:31.334
I wouldn't say all Brazilians
are like that but I am.

00:03:31.334 --> 00:03:37.267
So, after that I ended up
going to Cincinnati and,

00:03:37.267 --> 00:03:39.133
I know they're going to win
because I'm going to make sure

00:03:39.133 --> 00:03:44.567
he has a great night before.
[ Laughter ]

00:03:44.567 --> 00:03:46.367
I'm going to make sure.
-Alright.

00:03:46.367 --> 00:03:48.400
You guys heard it first.
There you go.

00:03:48.400 --> 00:03:50.834
Peyton Manning didn't say that,
you know?

00:03:50.834 --> 00:03:52.734
[ Laughter ]
-I didn't know anything

00:03:52.734 --> 00:03:55.567
about football, I actually
thought it was soccer

00:03:55.567 --> 00:03:58.667
because we call soccer football
in Brazil.

00:03:58.667 --> 00:04:01.033
-I know. Exactly.
-So I didn't know anything,

00:04:01.033 --> 00:04:03.400
I needed to search, but now I
know everything.

00:04:03.400 --> 00:04:04.868
He's going to have
a great night,

00:04:04.868 --> 00:04:06.934
and he's going to win next day.
You can bet all your money.

00:04:06.934 --> 00:04:10.968
-There you go. Right there.

00:04:10.968 --> 00:04:16.033
"Boys Don't Cry." It's a jam.
I love it. Everyone loves it.

00:04:16.033 --> 00:04:18.734
You're going to perform it for
us later.

00:04:18.734 --> 00:04:21.801
You were saying backstage
that this is not

00:04:21.801 --> 00:04:23.667
what it started out as,
this song.

00:04:23.667 --> 00:04:27.801
It was going to be more of a,
like, a disco type of jam or --

00:04:27.801 --> 00:04:30.634
-Yeah, it's more like, when I
was a teenager,

00:04:30.634 --> 00:04:33.601
I liked this rock vibe.
This kind of -- you know?

00:04:33.601 --> 00:04:34.801
-Yeah.
-And I wanted to

00:04:34.801 --> 00:04:36.667
bring this back,
I loved Panic! At The Disco,

00:04:36.667 --> 00:04:38.467
so that was my reference for
this song.

00:04:38.467 --> 00:04:40.801
-Love Panic! At The Disco.
-Yeah, I love it.

00:04:40.801 --> 00:04:43.467
-And it turned into this --
-Yeah, 'cause here's the deal,

00:04:43.467 --> 00:04:45.167
I started doing a rhythm in
Brazil.

00:04:45.167 --> 00:04:47.267
It suffers a lot of prejudice,
it's funk --

00:04:47.267 --> 00:04:49.801
it's kind of like hip hop
in '90s for America.

00:04:49.801 --> 00:04:52.400
Suffers a lot of prejudice
because it comes from the ghetto

00:04:52.400 --> 00:04:54.767
and the poor people
in the communities.

00:04:54.767 --> 00:04:57.701
So, people used to think,
"Oh, she shakes her ass

00:04:57.701 --> 00:04:58.868
so she's dumb."

00:04:58.868 --> 00:05:01.701
And I wanted to show
a different side.

00:05:01.701 --> 00:05:03.767
Like, yeah, I shake my ass,
but I can be smart.

00:05:03.767 --> 00:05:06.234
And I can do other rhythms.
You know?

00:05:06.234 --> 00:05:07.367
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:05:07.367 --> 00:05:08.934
-Absolutely.
You know what you're doing.

00:05:08.934 --> 00:05:11.467
I can sing rock.
-Yeah.

00:05:11.467 --> 00:05:13.067
I think you know
what you're doing, buddy.

00:05:13.067 --> 00:05:15.234
I really do.

00:05:15.234 --> 00:05:17.534
The video, by the way, I loved,
you directed it.

00:05:17.534 --> 00:05:18.734
-Yeah.
-Which also I love that

00:05:18.734 --> 00:05:20.100
you did that too.
You're like, "Oh, no, I'm not

00:05:20.100 --> 00:05:22.367
just going to put a video out.
I'm going to direct it."

00:05:22.367 --> 00:05:24.234
-Yeah,
'cause whenever I cut the song,

00:05:24.234 --> 00:05:25.767
I had so many ideas
for it.

00:05:25.767 --> 00:05:29.133
And I love movies, all my
reference I bring from movies,

00:05:29.133 --> 00:05:32.367
because I think it helps me to
not go through

00:05:32.367 --> 00:05:34.334
a place that other singers
are going.

00:05:34.334 --> 00:05:37.067
So, I just got reference from
movies I love I love,

00:05:37.067 --> 00:05:41.434
like, "Runaway Bride,"
"Harry Potter," "Beetlejuice."

00:05:41.434 --> 00:05:43.734
-"Beetlejuice"
I love that you did that.

00:05:43.734 --> 00:05:46.300
But I mean, all, like,
gorgeous versions of everything

00:05:46.300 --> 00:05:47.534
you just mentioned,
but yeah.

00:05:47.534 --> 00:05:50.601
-Yeah, that's "Titanic," that's
"Beetlejuice."

00:05:50.601 --> 00:05:53.334
But then I do, like, the
ex-boyfriends run away from me

00:05:53.334 --> 00:05:55.767
in the other scene because I
have, like 50 ex-boyfriends

00:05:55.767 --> 00:05:58.467
and they were all chasing me.
[ Laughter ]

00:05:58.467 --> 00:06:01.000
-Oh, my God
-So I wanted to reproduce

00:06:01.000 --> 00:06:02.167
my real life.
-Uh...

00:06:02.167 --> 00:06:03.901
-I say "Boys Don't Cry"
just in the title,

00:06:03.901 --> 00:06:07.234
but in the song they cry
'cause that's how they feel.

00:06:07.234 --> 00:06:08.934
-That's right.
That's exactly right.

00:06:08.934 --> 00:06:10.234
That's how they feel, yeah.
-Yeah.

00:06:10.234 --> 00:06:12.234
-'Cause, yeah, you would cry,
too, yeah if you --

00:06:12.234 --> 00:06:15.367
-I don't [bleep] for a guy.
-What?

00:06:15.367 --> 00:06:17.701
-I don't cry for the guys.

00:06:17.701 --> 00:06:19.834
They cry for me,
I don't cry for them.

00:06:19.834 --> 00:06:22.901
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:06:22.901 --> 00:06:24.734
-You're making me emotional.

00:06:24.734 --> 00:06:26.100
You're making me emotional
right now

00:06:26.100 --> 00:06:28.567
and I promised I wouldn't cry.
[ Laughter ]

00:06:28.567 --> 00:06:29.901
I'm so happy you're here.

00:06:29.901 --> 00:06:32.934
Congrats on every single little
new record breaking

00:06:32.934 --> 00:06:36.367
smashing thing you keep doing.
Just don't stop. Don't stop.

00:06:36.367 --> 00:06:37.801
Keep doing everything
you're doing.

00:06:37.801 --> 00:06:39.501
I love you,
and please come back whenever.

00:06:39.501 --> 00:06:42.000
Anitta, everybody.
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:06:42.000 --> 00:06:44.634
"Boys Don't Cry"
is available now.

